    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d279">

                <pb facs="0362" n="350" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg350"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.0040/178a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Fish</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-04-06T18:00:00-04:00">April 6, 1942—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>376. With reference to Department’s telegram today regarding exchange at Lourenço
                        Marques<anchor n="65" xml:id="d279-f1"/> please take any corresponding
                    measures which may seem advisable to you regarding forthcoming exchange at
                    Lisbon informing Department of such action and giving Department benefit of such
                    suggestions in the matter as may occur to you from time to time.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d279-f1" n="65" xml:id="d279-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 375, April 6, 5 p.m., to the Minister in Portugal, <ref
                        target="#pg410">p. 410</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
